{"format":1,"seq":321,"writes":[{"type":"document.change","id":2,"content":{"version":3,"kind":"delta","ops":[["p",["generation","message","content"],1,0,[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01P2VSnxDcfg25qTQfe1sMpX","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Start interactive Pi in tmux with the raw-call fixture provider and run prompt\"}\nasync ({ shell: { exec } }) => {\n  const script = String.raw`\nset -e\ncommand -v tmux >/dev/null\nROOT=$(mktemp -d /tmp/pit-raw-XXXXXX); mkdir -p $ROOT/home $ROOT/agent $ROOT/work\necho $ROOT > /tmp/pit-raw-root\nS=$ROOT/tmux.sock\nNODE=$(dirname \"$(command -v node)\")\nCMD=\"env -i PATH=$NODE:/usr/bin:/bin HOME=$ROOT/home PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR=$ROOT/agent TERM=xterm-256color LANG=C.UTF-8 PI_OFFLINE=1 PI_TELEMETRY=0 node $PWD/node_modules/@earendil"}}]],["a",["generation","message","content",0,"thinking"]," fixture provider, I'll run my own tmux session directly with the raw provider, checking if tmux is available and scripting prompts and pane captures. I'm noting that this raw provider only emits toolcall_start/end without deltas, so Pi's message_update fires on toolcall_start with empty args, creating a row.\n\nI also need to register the model with `--provider raw-fixture --model fixture`, and after running I'll press ctrl+o to expand the tool output view.\n\n"],["a",["generation","message","content",0,"thinkingSignature"],""],["a",["generation","message","content",1,"arguments","code"],"-works/pi-coding-agent/dist/bundle/cli.js -ne -e $PWD/src/index.ts -e $PWD/test/support/raw-call-provider.js --no-skills --no-context-files --no-prompt-templates --offline --provider raw-fixture --model fixture --session-dir $ROOT/sessions;"]]}}]}